                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[b]Kindly made by you of need[/b]\n\nThis is the last sentence in the \"intro\" section of the game which consists of a text explaining the background story. Apparently, we are the guinea pigs of a scientist and since we are inmates the doctor got special approval so that he can sacrifice the prisoners of the institution. The experiment is simple: we are chased by a demon and our job is to escape.\n\nAgain, the above is literally taken from the intro text. I picked a random sentence since most have typographical errors. We are only talking about a handful of sentences so you can guess how much time was spent with doing some quality check after the \"development\" was over. As for development: due to the typos and awfulness of the rest of the game I have to assume that this is one of those \"lovely\" Unity-asset-turned-into-video-game examples. Since another language selection is possible I assume the developers are not native English so they quickly used Google Translate to have the English translation from their mother tongue done for the \"intro\".\n\n[b]But what is HJ Sacrifice really?[/b]\n\nA mess. Nothing more, nothing less. We walk around looking for the exit. Occasionally a demon appears and runs towards us. The only thing we can do is to open cell doors and hide. Usually, the demon doesn't disappear so this option to hide is quite disappointing. Also, why are we unable to sprint? 3 hits and we are done. Back to main menu, hit play, watch the \"cutscene\" again, start over, rinse and repeat. \n\nThe demon's head often does some clipping as does our body when it comes to objects. Our protagonist constantly wants to climb over objects (desks, chairs, computer consoles, etc.). If he is unable to do so the clipping will suffice. At one point I managed to clip through the rusty objects in front of me to be able to find safe haven between 2 bunks. We have a flashlight but it usually works when we are close to walls i.e. the light appears only on them. Otherwise it is as if the light was constantly flickering.\n\n[b]Do not look behind you and run[/b]\n\nSays the store page but running is not an option. In fact, the Unity start-up screen tells us we have \"fire\" as an action button along with jumping. Neither works - for the latter our character starts by making an effort then he quickly lands as if he hit his head. Several options are available for graphics (from the very low to ultra) but none of them show any difference.\n\nEvade this game at any cost.",
